    "narrative": "The optimal lineup for Ghost Ride the WHIP today leans heavily into favorable matchups against mediocre pitching staffs. **Corbin Carroll** (79.46) headlines the squad, benefiting from an advantageous platoon dynamic and the #2 spot in the order against a vulnerable A. Abbott. Similarly, **Tyler Soderstrom** (75.99) and **Jose Caballero** (75.83) are high-ceiling plays; **Soderstrom** secures a massive boost from a projected middle-of-the-order presence against Tomoyuki Sugano, while **Caballero** leverages a rare +13% platoon edge to anchor the outfield. **Josh Naylor** (72.85) remains a pillar at 1B, capitalizing on a soft SP_xERA of 4.92, providing the core stability required to offset the volatility of our lower-slot starters.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the card involved **Travis Bazzana**, whose 46.22 score made him the \"first man out.\" While his #1 batting order slot provided a +10% boost, the optimizer favored the efficiency of **Kyle Karros** and **Alex Freeland**, as their specific platoon advantages outweighed the benefit of **Bazzana** hitting atop the lineup against Mize. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Max Muncy**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Henry Bolte**, and **Kyle Karros**, as their inclusion remains dependent on unconfirmed \"Lineup Pending\" statuses. Should these players shift lower in their respective lineups, we may see a dip in their effective scores, necessitating a mid-day pulse check on the roster. Finally, keep an eye on **Austin Riley** (53.34); while his score is marginal, the combination of his power profile and the 92% SB-friendly slow delivery of F. Peralta gives him a subtle edge over our deeper bench options.",
